WEBVTT

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.000
"Taking On the 2nd-Term Midterms!"

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.292
"Taking On the 2nd-Term Midterms!"
All right, class! The second-term midterms are just two weeks away!

00:00:10.292 --> 00:00:13.208
"Special Training to Improve in Your Worst Subjects"
All right, class! The second-term midterms are just two weeks away!

00:00:13.208 --> 00:00:15.958
The time has come at last
to surpass the A Class!

00:00:15.958 --> 00:00:19.042
Let's go into this red-hot! Hot! Hot!

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:20.292
That's oppressively hot!

00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:20.667
"Mathematics"
That's oppressively hot!

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.625
"Mathematics"
Ever since we dodged Asano's trap at the sports festival,

00:00:23.625 --> 00:00:27.667
"Mathematics"
we've been able to focus all our efforts on our midterms.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.417
"Mathematics"
At the same time,

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:32.667
we were all a little... restless, somehow.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:33.167
"Japanese History"
we were all a little... restless, somehow.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:37.292
"Japanese History"
Five months left until Koro Sensei's assassination deadline.

00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:40.708
We were only growing more impatient.

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:42.000
It's payback time!

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.167
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:01.000
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.417
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:09.083
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:11.833
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:15.625
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:01:15.625 --> 00:01:19.625
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:22.583
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:27.792
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:01:27.792 --> 00:01:33.375
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:38.792
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:01:38.792 --> 00:01:44.292
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:01:44.292 --> 00:01:46.917
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:01:46.917 --> 00:01:49.583
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:52.417
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:55.000
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.708
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:01:57.708 --> 00:02:00.417
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:03.250
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:08.208
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:15.958
"Sixth Period: Before & After Time"
"by Taiga Okajima"

00:02:19.625 --> 00:02:21.000
--What a rush!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.458
--Yesss!
--What a rush!

00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:27.292
How's this for the shortest way to the station?

00:02:27.292 --> 00:02:29.458
It's the best!

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.792
Wait up, guys!

00:02:31.792 --> 00:02:34.583
--No parkour outside of class!
--No sweat!

00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:39.333
The sports festival showed 'em:
we're no ordinary students!

00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:41.417
We just might pull off that assassination!

00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:43.708
What a shortcut!

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.125
What was that noise?!

00:03:05.125 --> 00:03:07.917
Oh, no! I'll call an ambulance!

00:03:11.042 --> 00:03:11.542
"To Emergency Reception"

00:03:11.542 --> 00:03:15.042
"To Emergency Reception"
A hairline fracture of the right femur.

00:03:15.042 --> 00:03:19.208
It's mild enough that he should be
up and walking in a week or so,

00:03:19.208 --> 00:03:22.042
but given that you kids are a state secret,

00:03:22.042 --> 00:03:26.167
my men are negotiating a gag order
and an out-of-court settlement.

00:03:26.708 --> 00:03:28.458
We...

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:38.042
K-Koro Sensei...

00:03:38.042 --> 00:03:40.875
B-But it was such a narrow street...

00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:44.333
Who'd ever expect an old man
to be riding his bike down there?

00:03:44.333 --> 00:03:45.542
He's right.

00:03:45.542 --> 00:03:49.292
I <i>do </i>think that what we did was wrong...

00:03:49.292 --> 00:03:52.792
But we did it to sharpen up our skills.

00:03:52.792 --> 00:03:57.250
You just don't get the pressure
and panic of havin' to save the Earth.

00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:07.042
Will you report that as injuring the students?

00:04:07.042 --> 00:04:10.375
I'll overlook it this once.

00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:14.042
I knew the risks when I introduced
that high-level training...

00:04:14.042 --> 00:04:17.958
It may have been too soon for you after all.

00:04:17.958 --> 00:04:20.125
It's my fault.

00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:25.958
Sir...

00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:27.292
We're sorry.

00:04:27.292 --> 00:04:29.958
--We're really sorry.
--We screwed up.

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:34.167
You may have grown too strong.

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:36.042
Drunk on your own power,

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:40.500
you forgot to put yourself in the shoes
of someone weaker than you.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.750
That makes you no different
than the students on the main campus.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:50.875
It hurt to be chastised like that,
but what could we say in reply?

00:04:50.875 --> 00:04:55.292
Is this what it means to make a mistake?

00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:01.708
The midterms are now
exactly two weeks away.

00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:05.542
I forbid any of you from studying for them.

00:05:05.542 --> 00:05:07.167
It's not a punishment.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:10.708
There are simply other things
you should be studying first.

00:05:10.708 --> 00:05:14.833
I'm responsible, too,
for having forgotten to teach them.

00:05:14.833 --> 00:05:15.375
If you could please accept this offer, Mr. Matsukata...

00:05:15.375 --> 00:05:17.750
"Mr. Matsukata"
If you could please accept this offer, Mr. Matsukata...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.000
"Mr. Matsukata"
I will not!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.417
I'll be cooped up in here for two weeks!

00:05:22.417 --> 00:05:25.333
The usual restitution
won't be enough for those brats.

00:05:25.333 --> 00:05:28.208
I'll need, say...
some kind of unprecedented... hmm...

00:05:28.208 --> 00:05:30.625
...bowing and scraping, say, or...

00:05:31.083 --> 00:05:31.458
"Get well soon! --Koro Sensei"

00:05:31.458 --> 00:05:37.750
"Get well soon! --Koro Sensei"
What the--? Who put all these flowers here all of a sudden?

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:39.125
I-I'm so sorry!

00:05:39.125 --> 00:05:40.750
"Apology"
I-I'm so sorry!

00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:46.167
Ten-billion-yen-bounty me and my students

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:46.417
have made so much trouble!

00:05:46.417 --> 00:05:48.292
"Apology"
have made so much trouble!

00:05:55.833 --> 00:05:58.750
Listen to this, children!

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:03.000
Principal Matsukata has been hurt,
so he can't work for a while.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:03.917
Whaaat?

00:06:03.917 --> 00:06:04.917
He got hurt?

00:06:04.917 --> 00:06:07.375
Poor Mr. Principal!

00:06:07.375 --> 00:06:10.083
So instead, these young men and women

00:06:10.083 --> 00:06:14.125
will do anything we need
for the next two weeks!

00:06:14.708 --> 00:06:17.208
Okay!

00:06:17.208 --> 00:06:18.625
Hmph.

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:20.875
Give me a break.

00:06:20.875 --> 00:06:22.458
--How'd we wind up with collective responsibility
--She's a witch!

00:06:22.458 --> 00:06:23.583
--How'd we wind up with collective responsibility
--I'm scared...

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.500
--when we had nothing to do with this?
--We gotta get rid of her.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.958
What a disgrace.

00:06:26.958 --> 00:06:28.750
He's really chomping on you!

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.625
We all got a sticky slap in the face, too.

00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:33.292
--Forgive me.
--He said he has to treat us all equally to keep things fair.

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:34.792
--I'm sorry. Forgive me.
--He said he has to treat us all equally to keep things fair.

00:06:34.792 --> 00:06:36.083
--Forgive me.
--He said he has to treat us all equally to keep things fair.

00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:37.333
Sorry about this.

00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:42.917
It's okay--we should have realized
someone could get hurt.

00:06:42.917 --> 00:06:46.667
I guess I might have
supervisory responsibility...

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:49.708
...as the trainer of this goofy circus troupe.

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:50.667
Hey!

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:54.917
Well, we can do some
stealth studying at home.

00:06:54.917 --> 00:07:00.750
Two weeks of unpaid work as a condition
for keeping the E Class's secret?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.375
A small price to pay for that bounty.

00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:06.417
Takebayashi...

00:07:06.417 --> 00:07:09.750
That'd be pretty astute if he weren't
standing there in his underpants.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:12.667
Lots of rambunctious kids here.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:16.375
So what exactly are you
planning to do for us, now?

00:07:16.375 --> 00:07:19.000
Barging in on us <i>en masse</i>...

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:24.167
Reckon you can at least work off
the oxygen you're taking up?

00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:26.625
And we've got some harsh kids, too!

00:07:26.625 --> 00:07:30.000
Uh-oh--Sis Sakura is in a bad mood.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Yeah...

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.208
These guys are gonna get murdered.

00:07:33.208 --> 00:07:35.250
She's been here five years--
the oldest kid around.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:38.542
And spent two of those years
resisting school control!

00:07:38.542 --> 00:07:41.208
Sis Sakura, the elite NEET!

00:07:41.208 --> 00:07:43.292
Something sure set you guys off.

00:07:43.292 --> 00:07:46.667
You make it sound cool and all,
but really, she just doesn't go to school.

00:07:46.667 --> 00:07:50.292
First, have you got what it takes to work?

00:07:50.292 --> 00:07:53.292
--Hey, uh--
--Let's just see, shall we? Hmm?

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:57.458
Aw! That part of the floor is no good!

00:07:57.458 --> 00:07:59.333
Aren't you getting it fixed?

00:07:59.333 --> 00:08:02.833
I mean... this building is pretty decrepit.

00:08:02.833 --> 00:08:04.958
We don't have the money.

00:08:04.958 --> 00:08:08.333
Any waitlisted student,
any child not attending primary school--

00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:11.458
our principal takes them in at rock-bottom rates.

00:08:11.458 --> 00:08:12.167
"Delicious Spring Water" "Barley Tea"

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:14.667
"Delicious Spring Water" "Barley Tea"
He can't even hire enough staff,

00:08:14.667 --> 00:08:16.750
"Delicious Spring Water" "Barley Tea"
so he winds up working the hardest.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.083
Twenty-eight of us for two weeks...

00:08:22.083 --> 00:08:23.833
I bet we could get some stuff done.

00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:25.583
Sure we could!

00:08:25.583 --> 00:08:26.417
Yeah!

00:08:26.417 --> 00:08:30.583
Okay, guys, let's divvy up
the duties and work in his stead!

00:08:30.583 --> 00:08:32.083
First, a strategy meeting!

00:08:32.083 --> 00:08:33.708
Got it!

00:08:35.583 --> 00:08:38.292
"Young Leaf Park"

00:08:38.792 --> 00:08:42.667
Please stop, Sir Karma!
You mustn't hurt anyone else!

00:08:42.667 --> 00:08:46.500
No, princess! I must drive out this monster!

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.542
Otherwise, peace will
ne'er return to our kingdom!

00:08:49.542 --> 00:08:51.292
Karma, you jerk...

00:08:51.292 --> 00:08:53.708
The script says "no contact"!

00:08:53.708 --> 00:08:57.458
Or was smackin' me around
your plan all along?!

00:08:57.458 --> 00:08:59.958
Wow... such realistic action!

00:08:59.958 --> 00:09:03.125
Yeah--and that lady's acting
really sucks me in!

00:09:03.125 --> 00:09:04.417
Hey!

00:09:04.417 --> 00:09:06.583
T-To your rest, monster!

00:09:07.917 --> 00:09:12.583
The mage's chloroform
put the monster to sleep unhurt.

00:09:12.583 --> 00:09:15.042
And they all lived happily ever after
with the power of chemistry!

00:09:15.042 --> 00:09:17.167
That's sneaky!

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:21.000
All right, children,
clap your hands if you liked that!

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.833
Kayano's great with kids.

00:09:22.833 --> 00:09:23.750
Yeah.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:23.958
"Mutsubishi Cement Corp."
Yeah.

00:09:23.958 --> 00:09:26.375
"Mutsubishi Cement Corp."
She knows how to read the room--

00:09:26.375 --> 00:09:27.708
"Mutsubishi Cement Corp."
and she's close to their size.

00:09:27.708 --> 00:09:30.292
"Mutsubishi Cement Corp."
So what are we heavy lifters supposed to do?

00:09:30.292 --> 00:09:33.417
"Mutsubishi Cement Corp."
Chiba's putting together some blueprints with Ritsu.

00:09:33.417 --> 00:09:36.000
Okay, leave the decorations to us!

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.375
Ready, and...

00:09:37.375 --> 00:09:38.708
Wow!

00:09:38.708 --> 00:09:39.625
I'll lend it to you.

00:09:39.625 --> 00:09:40.833
Yay!

00:09:40.833 --> 00:09:43.000
What a cute kitty cat!

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.625
I wonder if it's lost.

00:09:45.625 --> 00:09:49.167
What a huge help, having the students
from a prestigious junior high

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:51.625
look over their work one-on-one!

00:09:51.625 --> 00:09:55.458
Oh, no, no, miss--
we're the bottom of the barrel.

00:09:55.458 --> 00:09:57.167
Please don't expect much.

00:09:57.167 --> 00:09:58.917
"Third Grade"

00:09:59.625 --> 00:10:00.250
"Lesson 1: Addition and Subtraction"

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:03.958
"Lesson 1: Addition and Subtraction"
This girl <i>is </i>a bit behind in her studies.

00:10:03.958 --> 00:10:08.667
It's bound to happen if she stays here
instead of going on to primary school.

00:10:08.667 --> 00:10:10.375
Let's see...

00:10:10.375 --> 00:10:12.417
How can I explain these equations

00:10:12.417 --> 00:10:15.208
so even a primary-school kid
can understand it?

00:10:15.208 --> 00:10:18.125
Hmm. Teaching's tough.

00:10:18.125 --> 00:10:20.500
Make it snappy, Nagisa!

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:24.167
Weren't you supposed to
get me to Tokyo University?!

00:10:24.167 --> 00:10:25.833
S-Sorry...

00:10:25.833 --> 00:10:27.125
Hmph!

00:10:27.125 --> 00:10:28.917
Uh, hey...

00:10:29.542 --> 00:10:32.667
Why did you stop going to school?

00:10:32.667 --> 00:10:33.708
Huh?

00:10:33.708 --> 00:10:34.042
"Garbage" "Go home!" "Dummy" "Buh-bye!"
Huh?

00:10:34.042 --> 00:10:39.083
"Garbage" "Go home!" "Dummy" "Buh-bye!"
Bullying, of course--bullying! The typical stupid kind!

00:10:40.375 --> 00:10:42.542
I don't get people...

00:10:42.542 --> 00:10:46.000
Kids that age should be innocent and sweet.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.500
But once they get a little bigger and stronger,

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.625
I guess they use that strength to hurt people.

00:10:51.625 --> 00:10:53.625
Ouch.

00:10:53.625 --> 00:10:56.667
You're thinking it, too, aren't you?

00:10:56.667 --> 00:10:58.583
"Don't run away."

00:10:58.583 --> 00:11:02.875
"If you don't like it, go to school
and get stronger yourself."

00:11:02.875 --> 00:11:06.042
Just like Mom and Dad say.

00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:08.542
Well,

00:11:08.542 --> 00:11:13.375
you look weaker than me,
so you probably don't understand.

00:11:13.375 --> 00:11:16.167
Here, kitty-kitty!

00:11:17.917 --> 00:11:19.667
Oh, dear...

00:11:19.667 --> 00:11:22.000
Can't the kitty cat get down?

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:26.417
It's so little, it probably hasn't
climbed a lot of trees yet.

00:11:26.417 --> 00:11:31.000
See what happens when you
pluck up the courage to climb?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:34.083
The higher you get, the more dangerous it is.

00:11:34.083 --> 00:11:38.042
What's the harm in
staying down on<i> terra firma</i>?

00:11:39.875 --> 00:11:42.208
This is one clichéd mess.

00:11:42.208 --> 00:11:44.458
I'll go.

00:11:44.458 --> 00:11:46.625
Okajima--we'll do it like in the pole-toppling.

00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:47.917
Okay!

00:11:47.917 --> 00:11:50.417
Gotta make sure it's safe down below.

00:11:50.417 --> 00:11:52.167
Sakura...

00:11:53.125 --> 00:11:56.000
If that treetop is school,

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.875
and the ground is this place here...

00:11:58.875 --> 00:12:01.708
--...we all found our strength down on the ground.

00:12:01.708 --> 00:12:03.833
--Okay, all set!
--...we all found our strength down on the ground.

00:12:10.875 --> 00:12:14.333
While looking up...
and getting looked down on...

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:16.625
...we learned plenty about
how scary heights were

00:12:16.625 --> 00:12:19.083
before we started climbing.

00:12:19.083 --> 00:12:22.750
That's why we can go our own way now.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.000
Gotcha!

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.375
Yowch!

00:12:25.375 --> 00:12:30.458
Still... somewhere along the way
we forgot our fear of heights,

00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:34.458
so we do still fall to the ground now and then.

00:12:34.458 --> 00:12:36.167
So learn here.

00:12:36.167 --> 00:12:40.583
You can go on to school
once you have a game plan.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.833
That's my secret lesson, from me to you.

00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:48.583
Nagisa...

00:12:48.917 --> 00:12:52.917
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Kaede Kayano"

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:53.875
"Young Leaf Park"

00:12:53.875 --> 00:12:56.500
"Young Leaf Park"
Our work here was full of firsts.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:56.958
"Canola Oil" "Cholesterol Free"
Our work here was full of firsts.

00:12:56.958 --> 00:12:58.708
"Canola Oil" "Cholesterol Free"
That's why, while learning so much we wouldn't cover in school,

00:12:58.708 --> 00:13:01.083
That's why, while learning so much we wouldn't cover in school,

00:13:01.083 --> 00:13:04.500
the two weeks were over in a flash.

00:13:08.333 --> 00:13:13.625
Thank you so much for hearing us out.

00:13:13.625 --> 00:13:14.667
Hmph.

00:13:14.667 --> 00:13:18.208
When you said it was to
make your students more well-rounded,

00:13:18.208 --> 00:13:21.583
well, as a fellow educator, I couldn't say no.

00:13:21.583 --> 00:13:26.792
I hope that wooden ranch hasn't collapsed
under the weight of those brats.

00:13:26.792 --> 00:13:29.125
Hmm? Oh!

00:13:29.125 --> 00:13:31.000
"Young Leaf Park"
Before!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.042
After!

00:13:34.042 --> 00:13:36.833
What's the meaning of this?!

00:13:36.833 --> 00:13:39.625
A house built with trees
culled from the E Class's mountain

00:13:39.625 --> 00:13:42.792
and from discarded lumber:

00:13:42.792 --> 00:13:46.292
This was once a cramped
and humble preschool building...

00:13:49.667 --> 00:13:52.083
But what's this?

00:13:52.083 --> 00:13:55.917
It's now a roomy and
substantial multipurpose space!

00:13:55.917 --> 00:13:59.667
Oh, my... in only two weeks?

00:13:59.667 --> 00:14:03.417
Computerized calculations
mean it's perfectly sturdy.

00:14:03.417 --> 00:14:07.833
New pillars now shore up the entire
near-crumbling main building.

00:14:07.833 --> 00:14:11.833
Our calculations were drawn
from architecture all over the world!

00:14:11.833 --> 00:14:16.417
The second floor is divided into
two rooms, one being a library

00:14:16.417 --> 00:14:20.375
where the kids can
focus on studying or reading.

00:14:20.375 --> 00:14:23.833
It's a simple construction,
given our limited time and resources.

00:14:23.833 --> 00:14:27.750
"Insects Illustrated" "Kaba and Deba"
We went through the neighborhood collecting used children's books.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:29.167
"Insects Illustrated" "Kaba and Deba"
Including mine!

00:14:29.167 --> 00:14:29.958
Including mine!

00:14:29.958 --> 00:14:34.125
The other room is an indoor playground.

00:14:34.125 --> 00:14:38.875
Careful placement of netting
and mats ensure safety,

00:14:38.875 --> 00:14:40.750
and since it's all out of the rain,

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:44.375
the equipment won't grow brittle
from corrosion or rust.

00:14:44.375 --> 00:14:46.375
These kids...

00:14:46.375 --> 00:14:48.958
Next up is the garage.

00:14:48.958 --> 00:14:51.458
The garage?

00:14:51.458 --> 00:14:52.833
Whoa!

00:14:52.833 --> 00:14:55.042
Oh, my goodness me!

00:14:55.042 --> 00:14:58.333
The tech squad has entirely
remodeled the principal's bicycle,

00:14:58.333 --> 00:15:00.875
whose front wheel was bent in the fall!

00:15:00.875 --> 00:15:03.917
Now it's an ultra-safe, high-load-bearing,

00:15:03.917 --> 00:15:06.875
electric-assisted three-wheeler!

00:15:06.875 --> 00:15:10.500
The rotating playscape upstairs
is connected to a battery charger.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:15.167
The bike was designed to draw
most of its power from that turning.

00:15:15.167 --> 00:15:16.333
In other words...

00:15:16.333 --> 00:15:19.167
the more children use the playscape,

00:15:19.167 --> 00:15:21.917
the more they'll help out their principal!

00:15:21.917 --> 00:15:24.000
This is all too perfect!

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:27.792
You've done far too well--
it's actually a little creepy!

00:15:27.792 --> 00:15:32.792
The principal's nostalgic old dentures
were reused in the trike's bell.

00:15:32.792 --> 00:15:35.583
No one needs <i>that </i>much attention to detail!

00:15:35.583 --> 00:15:37.208
Besides...

00:15:37.208 --> 00:15:39.542
You can bring all these <i>things </i>up to scratch,

00:15:39.542 --> 00:15:43.667
but if you didn't get in close
to these children's hearts...

00:15:43.667 --> 00:15:48.625
then I can't say you've
done your job these two weeks.

00:15:48.625 --> 00:15:50.542
Hey, Nagisa!

00:15:50.542 --> 00:15:51.083
"Math Test" "Score: 95/100"
Hey, Nagisa!

00:15:51.083 --> 00:15:52.292
"Math Test" "Score: 95/100"
Ta-da! I came in second!

00:15:52.292 --> 00:15:53.958
Ta-da! I came in second!

00:15:53.958 --> 00:15:56.583
Wow, that's great! Well done!

00:15:56.583 --> 00:15:59.000
I did just what you said!

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:02.417
I came in only for my math test,
like a sneak attack.

00:16:02.417 --> 00:16:05.042
I finished the test and left.

00:16:05.042 --> 00:16:09.000
And in the middle of a test,
the bullies couldn't do a thing.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:14.458
Yep! Apart from the teacher,
I didn't tell anyone I was leaving.

00:16:14.458 --> 00:16:20.292
Using your best attack <i>before</i>
your opponent can get into position:

00:16:20.292 --> 00:16:24.542
that's how we fight in the E Class, Sakura.

00:16:24.542 --> 00:16:28.125
Keep on using those hit-and-run tactics

00:16:28.125 --> 00:16:30.833
and you'll have more weapons
at your disposal in school.

00:16:30.833 --> 00:16:32.708
Th-Then...

00:16:33.708 --> 00:16:37.583
You'll teach me again sometime, right?

00:16:37.583 --> 00:16:39.167
Of course!

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.292
That's one scary dude.

00:16:42.292 --> 00:16:46.000
He's so oblivious--
that's what makes him so terrifying.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:51.375
You brats... I can't come up
with a single complaint.

00:16:51.375 --> 00:16:55.333
Oh, welcome back, Principal! Look at this!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:17:00.667
You all run back to school, now.

00:17:00.667 --> 00:17:03.417
You have some important work to attend to.

00:17:03.417 --> 00:17:04.833
Yes, sir!

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:14.750
--See you later!

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:16.167
--And so,
--See you later!

00:17:16.167 --> 00:17:19.417
our special lesson came to an end.

00:17:19.417 --> 00:17:21.917
However...

00:17:21.917 --> 00:17:25.208
...the midterms were the very next day.

00:17:26.375 --> 00:17:28.625
It was a disaster.

00:17:28.625 --> 00:17:32.792
The majority of the E Class
got booted out of the top spots.

00:17:35.167 --> 00:17:37.083
"Tomohito Sugino: 65th overall" "Taiga Okajima: 76th overall"
"Nagisa Shiota: 54th overall"

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.750
What a let-down.

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:40.833
"Teppai Araki: 4th overall" "Natsuhiko Koyama: 6th overall"
What a let-down.

00:17:40.833 --> 00:17:42.417
"Teppai Araki: 4th overall" "Natsuhiko Koyama: 6th overall"
Guess that first time was just a fluke, eh?

00:17:42.417 --> 00:17:44.250
"Gakushu Asano: 1st overall" "Teppai Araki: 4th overall"
Guess that first time was just a fluke, eh?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:44.958
"Gakushu Asano: 1st overall" "Teppai Araki: 4th overall"
We didn't even <i>need </i>to smash you at pole-toppling.

00:17:44.958 --> 00:17:45.333
"Gakushu Asano: 1st overall" "Ren Sakakibara: 3rd overall"
We didn't even <i>need </i>to smash you at pole-toppling.

00:17:45.333 --> 00:17:47.000
"Ren Sakakibara: 3rd overall" "Tomoya Seo: 5th overall"
We didn't even <i>need </i>to smash you at pole-toppling.

00:17:48.458 --> 00:17:52.083
Cat got your tongue? That's not surprising.

00:17:52.083 --> 00:17:54.875
At this school, grades are everything.

00:17:54.875 --> 00:17:58.000
Those on the bottom have
no right speaking to those at the top.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.417
Really?

00:17:59.417 --> 00:18:03.958
Then you can't say
anything to me, now, can you?

00:18:03.958 --> 00:18:05.958
Only one student in the E Class

00:18:05.958 --> 00:18:09.583
remained undaunted
by that two-week handicap.

00:18:09.583 --> 00:18:14.208
I didn't miss the traces
of major prep work at his house

00:18:14.208 --> 00:18:17.333
the day of the summer festival.

00:18:17.333 --> 00:18:17.500
I mean, our teacher'll probably be like,

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.000
"Karma Akabane: 2nd overall"
I mean, our teacher'll probably be like,

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:24.167
"Karma Akabane: 2nd overall"
"It doesn't count if you didn't come in <i>first</i>."

00:18:24.167 --> 00:18:26.208
Karma!

00:18:26.208 --> 00:18:28.167
Hasn't it dawned on you?

00:18:28.167 --> 00:18:31.167
I'm the only one who
gave it my all this time around.

00:18:31.167 --> 00:18:34.958
Everyone else was
pulling their punches for you.

00:18:34.958 --> 00:18:38.708
Said you'd have no standing
if you kept on losing.

00:18:38.708 --> 00:18:40.167
Say what?!

00:18:40.167 --> 00:18:44.500
But we won't go easy on you next time.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.292
C'mon!

00:18:48.667 --> 00:18:50.667
Karma...

00:18:50.667 --> 00:18:54.583
He really covered for us.

00:18:58.083 --> 00:19:02.208
We're so sorry for
all the trouble, Mr. Karasuma.

00:19:02.208 --> 00:19:05.542
All in a day's work. Don't worry about it.

00:19:05.542 --> 00:19:07.750
What about you?

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:11.000
Have you learned anything from this?

00:19:12.417 --> 00:19:16.500
It's not for our own money... or our grades.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:20.417
It reminded me that we can
use the strength we've gained

00:19:20.417 --> 00:19:22.500
for others, too.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:25.833
If we have the power to kill,
we can save the Earth.

00:19:25.833 --> 00:19:29.708
If we have academic ability,
we can help someone.

00:19:29.708 --> 00:19:32.500
And we won't use it so carelessly again.

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:35.250
We'll be careful--in lots of ways.

00:19:39.083 --> 00:19:43.083
Failure and frustration, too,
are sources of growth.

00:19:43.083 --> 00:19:46.667
Surely this will make them all stronger.

00:19:46.667 --> 00:19:48.083
They should just keep applying themselves

00:19:48.083 --> 00:19:51.125
to their studies and their assassination.

00:19:51.125 --> 00:19:52.500
Now, then...

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.958
Time for a little BBQ with
the <i>foie gras </i>I bought on the sly

00:19:54.958 --> 00:19:56.625
at a French farmer's market!

00:19:56.625 --> 00:20:00.375
At least I've kept <i>this </i>from my students!

00:20:05.583 --> 00:20:08.208
Wh-Where the heck did you come from?!

00:20:08.208 --> 00:20:13.000
Wow... that much of a drop,
and it didn't hurt a bit!

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:21.083
Wh-What's going on?
I barely have time to breathe!

00:20:21.083 --> 00:20:24.458
We wanted you to see this, Koro Sensei!

00:20:24.458 --> 00:20:28.000
New equipment from the government.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:32.083
I told them not to tip their hand...

00:20:32.083 --> 00:20:37.542
But they really wanted to show you
how they use their new powers.

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.875
We'll respond to your lessons
with an assassination.

00:20:42.875 --> 00:20:45.500
It's how we do things around here.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.708
We promise, Koro Sensei.

00:20:47.708 --> 00:20:53.917
We won't use this power
except to protect someone.

00:20:53.917 --> 00:20:56.667
You get full marks for that answer.

00:20:56.958 --> 00:20:58.083
"Assassination"

00:20:58.083 --> 00:21:01.625
"Assassination"
When I first came, I found only some stagnant bloodlust

00:21:01.625 --> 00:21:04.875
"Assassination"
here and there in the classroom.

00:21:04.875 --> 00:21:06.917
"Assassination"
There was little danger of being assassinated,

00:21:06.917 --> 00:21:08.917
"Assassination"
but it was a cold space.

00:21:08.917 --> 00:21:09.292
"Tentacle"
but it was a cold space.

00:21:09.292 --> 00:21:10.375
"Tentacle"
Now, though...

00:21:10.375 --> 00:21:11.083
Now, though...

00:21:11.083 --> 00:21:15.375
...the whole campus is
bubbling over with genial bloodlust!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:22.125
One day you, too,
will meet someone like that...

00:21:24.375 --> 00:21:29.167
Yes. I have so many of them now,
right before my eyes.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:48.000
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:53.375
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:53.375 --> 00:21:59.042
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:59.042 --> 00:22:04.208
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:04.208 --> 00:22:15.583
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.583 --> 00:22:21.167
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:21.167 --> 00:22:25.583
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.583 --> 00:22:32.417
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.417 --> 00:22:37.917
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:37.917 --> 00:22:43.417
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.417 --> 00:23:02.059
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
